    "title": "pandas.PeriodIndex.daysinmonth — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.PeriodIndex.daysinmonth#\n\n- \n*property* PeriodIndex.daysinmonth[source]#\n- The number of days in the month. Examples For Series: >>> period = pd.period_range('2020-1-1 00:00', '2020-3-1 00:00', freq='M') >>> s = pd.Series(period) >>> s 0 2020-01 1 2020-02 2 2020-03 dtype: period[M] >>> s.dt.days_in_month 0 31 1 29 2 31 dtype: int64 For PeriodIndex: >>> idx = pd.PeriodIndex([\"2023-01\", \"2023-02\", \"2023-03\"], freq=\"M\") >>> idx.days_in_month # It can be also entered as `daysinmonth` Index([31, 28, 31], dtype='int64')",
    "markdown_length": 528,
